course: dictionary
lesson: 15353
title: Solitude: being alone
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Solitude means being alone, usually in a quiet, peaceful way that you have chosen. «Maya loved the solitude of the early morning, when the house was silent.» Nobody else is awake, and Maya likes it that way.
explain: Look at the words around solitude for clues. «The lighthouse keeper lived in solitude on a rock far from the town.» Far from the town and on a rock tell you he was alone, and he lived that way on purpose. Solitude is about being alone, not about being sad.
explain: Solitude can also mean a lonely, empty place where few people go. This meaning is more formal and you will mostly meet it in stories and poems: «The wind howled over the solitude of the moor.» Ask yourself: does the sentence describe a place or a feeling? That will tell you which meaning to use.
fact: «Solitude» means being alone in a quiet, peaceful way that you have chosen.
fact: «Solitude» can also mean a lonely, empty place where few people go.
fact: Solitude is usually uncountable, so you say «some solitude» or «in solitude», not «a solitude».
fact: Useful phrases: in solitude, peace and solitude, enjoy solitude.
fact: Solitude is not the same as loneliness: loneliness is usually a sad feeling, but solitude can be chosen and peaceful.
exercise: «Maya loved the solitude of the early morning, when the house was silent.» What does solitude mean here? | A loud crowd of friends | A bad storm | *Quiet time alone | A long journey
exercise: «The lighthouse keeper lived in solitude on a rock far from the town.» Which words are clues that solitude means being alone? | with lots of friends | loud and busy | *far from the town | in a crowded city
exercise: «After the noisy party, Sam wanted some solitude to read his book.» Find and copy one word that means quiet time alone. | book | noisy | *solitude | party
test: «The wind howled over the solitude of the moor, where no one had walked for years.» Here solitude means a lonely, empty place. | a warm kitchen | a loud market | a school trip | *a lonely, empty place
test: Lena says solitude is the same as loneliness. Why is she only partly right? | Solitude means a crowd of people | Loneliness is always chosen | *Solitude can be chosen and peaceful, while loneliness is usually a sad feeling | Solitude and loneliness are exactly the same
exam: Which sentence uses solitude correctly? | The solitude was a cake from the shop | I enjoyed a solitude with my friends at the party | *She went for a walk in solitude to think about her day | Solitude is the name of a bright, happy game
